{'agent': 'diagnostics', 'brief': "Customer reports their Tamberwick vacuum keeps stopping mid-use and blinking a red light/indicator. No model number, purchase date, or error code was provided, and we have no order context for this contact. Customer's first name is unknown.

Please advise on: (1) what a blinking red indicator typically signifies across Tamberwick vacuum models, (2) the most likely causes of repeated mid-cycle shutdown (e.g. brush bar obstruction, filter blockage, overheating cutoff, battery/charging fault, dustbin seating), and (3) step-by-step troubleshooting the customer can do themselves, in order of likelihood.

Also note what diagnostic info we should ask the customer for to narrow it down (model number, blink pattern/count, whether it happens on battery or mains, how long it runs before stopping). Do not guess at specific error codes — if the blink pattern maps to distinct codes, tell us what to ask rather than assuming."}
